    "section_double_QrXmLg": {
      "type": "section-double",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_CGJjPK": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Holy Bible Scriptures",
            "text_size": 7,
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        },
        "text_wB8yCJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Revelation 19:14</strong></p><p>The armies of heaven were following him, riding on white horses and dressed in fine linen, white and pure.</p><p><strong>Revelation 3:4-18</strong></p><p>They will walk with me, dressed in white, for they are worthy. The one who is victorious will, like them, be dressed in white. </p><p><strong>Revelation 19:8</strong><br/>It was given to her to clothe herself in pure white linen, bright and clean; for the fine linen is the righteous acts of the saints.</p><p><strong>Revelation 7:9</strong></p><p>\"The Great Multitude in White Robes\" After this I looked, and there before me was a great multitude that no one could count, from every nation, tribe, people and language, standing before the throne and before the Lamb. They were wearing white robes and were holding palm branches in their hands.</p><p><strong>Revelation 15:6</strong></p><p>The seven angels who had the seven plagues came out of the temple, clothed in linen, clean and bright, and girded around their chests with golden sashes.<br/></p><p><strong>Exodus 39:28</strong></p><p>The turban and the special head coverings were made of fine linen, and the undergarments were also made of finely woven linen.</p><p><strong>Ezekiel 44:17-18</strong></p><p>They shall be clothed with linen garments. They shall have linen bonnets upon their heads and shall have linen breeches upon their loins.</p><p><strong>John 19:40</strong></p><p>They took the body of Jesus, and wound it in linen clothes with spices. (Messiah's burial cloth)</p><p><strong>Leviticus 16:4</strong></p><p>He shall put on the holy linen tunic, and the linen undergarments shall be next to his body, and he shall be girded with the linen sash and attired with the linen turban (these are holy garments). </p><p><strong>1 Chronicles 15:27</strong><br/>David was clothed with a robe of fine linen with all the Levites who were carrying the ark. David also wore an ephod of linen.</p><p><strong>Proverbs 31:13-24</strong></p><p>The Wife of Noble Character… She selects wool and flax; She is clothed in fine linen and purple. She makes linen garments, and sells them, and supplies robed sashes unto the merchants.</p><p></p>",
            "text_size": 3,
            "text_style": "font-body",
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        }
      },
